# The zone dnsd serves: names under `zone`, each a list of addresses
# (an IPv4 address answers A, an IPv6 one AAAA), all with one TTL.
#
# `node1` stays here as the fabric's bootstrap name (a joiner resolves its
# seed before it is a member of anything). Every other `nodeN` is left to
# the live overlay: the cluster dnsd, handed a fabric channel, answers
# `nodeN.moss.test` from fabsvc's membership (10.77.0.N/fdcc::N when up,
# NXDOMAIN when a known member is down), so those names track the mesh
# instead of a hardcoded list. The plain net-drill dnsd has no fabric and
# serves only what is written here.
{
  zone: moss.test
  ttl:  300
  names: {
    www:   [::1]
    node1: [10.77.0.1, fdcc::1]
    tls:   [10.0.2.2]
  }
}
